Z||000000||87FieroGTx||08-10-2001||09:01 PM|||| Would a BMW V-12 fit in a Fiero?<P> The V-12 will hook up to the same Porche trans that a SBC hooks to so shouldn't the V-12 hook to a Fiero trans??<P> My friend with the 3.8s/c just finished his Diablo SE kitcar and wanted to know if he could put the V-12 in transverse or if he has to put it in Longitudinal with a Porche 5 speed.<P> He bought the engine for $5,000 it has 380hp and 300tq and is prety light weight plus it sounds sweet and looks more like a diablo engine than a V-6<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||artherd||08-11-2001||02:25 AM||||I've oft thought about this...<P>In a diablo kit, the engine will fit for sure, no problem.<P>It will be closer in an otherwise 'stock' fiero, though with absolutely no accessories, and the pully shaved off, you might get there...<P>I decided to go with a Northstar v8 with a 5-speed for now, though I intend to revisit the BMW V12 once I can afford to do so  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>PS: I belive the 535 (525?) DOHC heads will bolt to the 6litre v12, though the exaust will be flipped on one (would require total fabrication of intake and exaust from the ground up.)  <P>The v12 is SOHC from the factory (one of the factors that stalled my attempt of this swap  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
